Question 1: Transaction Rate Limiter (Medium → Medium-Hard)
Problem

You are building a rate limiter for a banking API.

Each client can make at most N transactions in any rolling T-second window.

You are given:

clientId

timestamp (in seconds, increasing order)

limit = N

windowSize = T

Return true if the transaction is allowed, false if it should be rejected.

Constraints

Up to 1 million transactions

Must be efficient

Example
limit = 3, windowSize = 10

(client1, 1)  -> true
(client1, 2)  -> true
(client1, 3)  -> true
(client1, 11) -> true
(client1, 12) -> true
(client1, 13) -> true
(client1, 14) -> false

What they look for

Deque per client

Sliding window cleanup

O(1) amortized per call

Clean separation of logic


